    "fullText": "",
    "fullTextFormats": [],
    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "Amd §402, V & T L",
    "lawSection": "Vehicle and Traffic Law",
    "memo": "\n \nBILL NUMBER: S4849\n\nSPONSOR: REICHLIN-MELNICK\n \nTITLE OF BILL:\n\nAn act to amend the vehicle and traffic law, in relation to penalties\nfor purposefully obstructed license plates\n\n \nPURPOSE:\n\nTo discourage the purposeful obstruction of license plates.\n\n \nSUMMARY OF PROVISIONS:  The bill would increase the maximum fine for\nknowingly covering or coating a license plate with any artificial or\nsynthetic material or substance that conceals or obscures the plate, or\nthat distorts a recorded or photographic image of the plate.\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nThe current punishment for an obstructed license plate does little to\nprevent the problem. Criminals will intentionally cover their license\nplates to make it nearly impossible for law enforcement officials to\nidentify the vehicle or to stop them. This law would create an incentive\nto not cover a license plate.\n\n \nLEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\nNo prior Senate history.\n\n \nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS:\n\nNone.\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nThis act shall take effect on the first of November next succeeding the\ndate upon which it shall have become a law.\n",
    "multiSponsors": {
